==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Swashbuckler Kanna''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Fabled Adventure Girl Kanna''' at level 30 using [[Behemoth Stone]]s and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
While a little fragile and low on attack power against non-Dark enemies, this unit really shines against her targeted trait. Due to how [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark enemies]] usually work, 400 standing range is more than enough to outrange most Dark enemies; even [[Director Kurosawah]] can be hit with the help of stepping stones that normally already come in any Dark based stage. With multi-hit, varying area of damage and [[Surge Attack|Surge]] in her first attack, normally receiving an attack that would trigger her knockback is a positive, since that means she will restart her attacking animation and drop another Surge, so finding a [[Tackey]] or two among the enemy lines can work to your advantage. Be careful with stacks of these, though, as they can rip Kanna apart quite fast. Support from Talented [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer Cat]] is pretty useful, as they can target those pesky things with [[Wave Attack|waves]]. Finally, [[Two Can]] is probably the only bad matchup Kanna has against Dark, since she's not immune to waves.

The bad thing with Kanna is that the different areas her attacks and Surge land will most likely cause her to fail some of her attacks, however, since Dark enemies tend to have many knockbacks, her attacks can be chained against Dark enemies one knockback after the other, as well as spreading damage among melee and backliner enemies. Standard measures for [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance units]] that have blind spots should also be taken, but since her second attack hits as close as 250 from her, she has the chance of repelling pushers herself.

On a final note, she's part of the [[Dream Box (Combo)|Dream Box]] combo with [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] which just so happens to be one of the best combo slaves in the game, so you can combine combos like Dream Box and [[Working Vacation (Combo)|Working Vacation]] to get a +20% increase to Massive Damage with just 3 units. Heavy Assault C.A.T. can also gain Massive Damage through talents, further making this combo even deadlier.

==='''True Form'''===
Kanna's True Form doesn't add basic stats like extra health, attack power, knockback count, speed or cooldown, but she gains [[Behemoth Slayer]], as well as an upgrade to her Surge, going from Lvl.2 to Lvl.3 and increasing potential damage against non-Immune enemies. With all of this, she becomes an abuser of Dark/Behemoth enemies. At level 50, she can kill a 100% [[Ragin' Gory]] in just 1 attack cycle (assuming all three attacks connect)! And, although [[Casaurian Darkjo]] is immune to Surges, the multiplier of Massive Damage and Behemoth Slayer still applies, so if you could keep it away long enough, she'll melt through its 2 million HP quite fast.

In short, she'll be very useful for farming [[Catfruit#Behemoth stones|Behemoth Stones]] as one of the only Ubers with Behemoth Slayer, and her combination of backliner and super-backliner attacks with Surge may earn her a spot as a generalist in your deck. Do note she is still rather reliant on her Surges, and a great deal of Behemoths have resistances to Surge Attacks, but she still can help with those that don't.

==='''Talents'''===
Kanna's Talents leave a lot to be desired.

'''Speed Up''' is a very bad Talent. With this, Kanna will become suicidal and run faster than your meatshields. Then she'll die. Please don't get this Talent.

'''Survive''' isn't that bad, as having an extra chance to do something in the battle is always welcome. However, this talent costs 235 NP to max out, so it's absolutely a lower priority Talent to only get if you really like Kanna.

'''Slow Immunity''' is a little weird. On the anti-Dark side, the only enemies with Slow are two event enemies ([[Selena]] and [[Bears Be Back]]), and [[Le'Grim]]. On the Behemoth side, [[Crustaceous Scissorex]] will just kill Kanna, leaving only [[Lophiiformes Angaburu]] as her one relevant usage case in her niche. Outside of her niches, [[Croakley]] and [[Tarsiriel]] exist to give this Talent some usage. Overall, though, there's not really too much you can get out of this Talent.

Finally, Kanna has her stat talents. Kanna's health beforehand isn't too notable, so you'll want to focus on her Attack Talent to let her hit even higher damage numbers against Darks and Behemoths.

